* sg13g2-pll :: sim/sg13cmos5l-pfd-input-threshold (issue #403, spec row 2 / R-5)
* DC switching threshold of the committed SG13CMOS5L `pfd` REF input stage
* (../netlist-snapshots/pfd.spice, byte-identical to
* design/sg13cmos5l/netlist/pfd.spice).
*
* REF is swept 0 -> VDD with FB held low, so the reset path is inert and the
* REF edgedet (XED_UP) is the only input stage being exercised.  edgedet's
* OUT (the `set_up` net) is a ~5-gate-delay EDGE PULSE, not a level -- it
* responds where the XN1 nand2_hv sees X and the 5-inverter delayed leg XD5
* overlap high -- so it cannot be measured in a DC sweep.  The static
* thresholds reported are on the named internal nodes:
*   d1   -- the input inverter's output: its own trip point (V_M of inv_hv).
*   xd5  -- the delayed leg the NAND compares against; its trip point
*           (falling, since five inversions hang off X).
*   ntmp -- the NAND output; it dips below mid-rail only where X and XD5
*           overlap high in the sweep, so its crossing may not exist at
*           every corner (NA is meaningful there); ntmp_min over the sweep
*           is reported alongside.
* The edge decks (tb_pfd_edge.sp.tmpl) measure where the pulse stops being
* produced; the record names the node each number belongs to.
*
* Placeholders are substituted by testbench/threshold_grid.py, which also
* inserts the pre_osdi / num_threads lines into the .control block (a
* deck-list unit has no .spiceinit).

.lib $PDK_ROOT/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOShv.lib @CORNER_MOS@
.option scale=1 temp=@TEMP@

.include pfd_snap.spice

Vdd vdd 0 dc @VDD@
Vref ref 0 dc 0
Vfb  fb  0 dc 0

Xpfd ref fb up dn vdd 0 pfd

.dc Vref 0 @VDD@ @DSTEP@

.control
run
meas dc vth_d1   when v(xpfd.xed_up.d1)=@VMID@
meas dc vth_xd5  when v(xpfd.xed_up.xd5)=@VMID@
meas dc vth_ntmp when v(xpfd.xed_up.ntmp)=@VMID@
meas dc ntmp_min min v(xpfd.xed_up.ntmp)
print vth_d1 vth_xd5 vth_ntmp ntmp_min
.endc
.end
